Hi folks, a bit new to these packages but hoping to learn lots!

Has anyone made predictions from a zero-inflated gaussian model? When I tried to use predict(model, covars) I got an error saying:

"Error in predict.abund(out, X.0) : z.0.samples must be supplied for a zi-Gaussian model"

Note that predictions worked for a gaussian model, so I'm guessing that it is not an issue with the covariate matrix or the model itself. I think this means I need to use spOccupancy to build that binomial presence/absence model, use that to create the z.0.samples object that has binary predictions across my prediction dataset, and then predict() on that? But I'm unclear on how best to do that (fit a detection only spOccupancy object with same covars and use that to predict?). Or is there a way to predict the binary response from my abund() object itself without fitting a separate model?

If anyone has insight to share I would super appreciate it, thank you!

Jonathan

